WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.550
A cinema's new ticket
program has one rule:

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.630
adult ticket for ages 18 and over.

3
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:11.830
The developer tests it with
three ages: 10, 30, 50.

4
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.410
Every ticket is right.

5
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.490
Green ticks all round.

6
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:16.810
Opening night.

7
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:20.730
An 18-year-old buys a ticket
and is charged the child price.

8
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.530
It passed every test.

9
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.790
So how did it get this one wrong?

10
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.190
In this mission, you'll see how a program
can run without crashing and still give

11
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.490
wrong results.

12
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.170
And you'll learn to choose test
data that could expose errors:

13
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:37.370
values to accept, values
right on the limits,

14
00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.470
and values to reject.

15
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.730
Your mission: explain why the program
passed every test but still failed for an

16
00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:45.520
18-year-old.
